# Lesson 2, new hand: partner opens 2NT, you have 5. Student sits North.
title: Partner opens 2NT, you have 5
id: L02-23
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.4
student: N
board: 23
dealer: S
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  J84    Q52    9763   Q85
  E  T3     T98    JT2    AT972
  S  AQ5    AK73   KQ4    KJ6
  W  K9762  J64    A85    43

auction:
  S 2NT    = 21-22 points, balanced
  W Pass
  N 3NT*   = 4+ points: game
     key: 5 HCP opposite 21-22 makes at least 26. Bid game.
     not Pass: Did you count 5? With 4 or more opposite 2NT, raise to game.
     not *: With 4+ points opposite 2NT, the lesson says raise to 3NT.
  E Pass
  S Pass
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 2NT showed 21-22 points and a balanced hand. Your 5 points
  bring your side to at least 26, so you bid game. South is declarer,
  because she bid no-trump first, and so West will lead to the first
  trick.

play:
  1   W S6  N S4  E ST  S SQ
  2   S CJ  W C3  N C5  E CA
      note: Declarer's plan: drive out the ♣A, then take hearts, spades, clubs and a diamond. Dummy's two queens help.
  3   E DJ  S DQ  W DA  N D3
  4   W C4  N C8  E C9  S CK
  5   S H3  W H4  N HQ  E H8
      note: Now the hearts. Dummy's ♥Q first, the high card from the short side.
  6   N H2  E H9  S HK  W H6
      note: Back to declarer's ♥K.
  7   S HA  W HJ  N H5  E HT
      note: And the ♥A.
  8   S H7  W S2  N D6  E S3
      note: The hearts split evenly, so the last one is a winner.
  9   S C6  W S7  N CQ  E C2
      note: A club to dummy's ♣Q.
  10  N D7  E D2  S DK  W D5
      note: Back to declarer's ♦K.
  11  S SA  W S9  N S8  E C7
      note: The ♠A.
  12  S S5  W SK  N SJ  E DT
      note: Ten tricks are in. West's ♠K takes this one.
  13  W D8  N D9  E CT  S D4
      note: 10 tricks: 3NT made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: drive out the ♣A, then take the hearts, spades, clubs
  and a diamond.

  3NT made with an overtrick. Your ♥Q, ♣Q and last diamond all became
  tricks: even a few points matter opposite a 2NT opener.
